---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Hard Wax Albuquerque — ABQWax.ing"
  description="Hard wax Albuquerque: how hard wax works, hard wax vs soft wax, best uses, and aftercare. Plus ABQWax.ing, the Albuquerque waxing domain offered at $250,000."
  canonical="/hard-wax-albuquerque/"
  keywords="hard wax Albuquerque, hard wax vs soft wax, hard wax benefits, Albuquerque hard wax, ABQWax.ing"
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Hard Wax Albuquerque', path: '/hard-wax-albuquerque/' },
  ]}
>
  <Header />

  <main class="flex-1">
    <section class="border-b border-ink-100 bg-ink-950">
      <div class="container-narrow py-16 sm:py-24">
        <p class="text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-widestx text-gold-400">Albuquerque · Hard Wax · Method</p>
        <h1 class="mt-3 max-w-3xl font-display text-4xl font-semibold leading-tight text-white sm:text-6xl">
          Hard wax in Albuquerque, and why it wins
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-100/85 sm:text-lg">
          Hard wax grips hair, not skin. That single difference defines the modern standard for Brazilian, bikini, and underarm work across Albuquerque.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-padding bg-white">
      <div class="container-narrow grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="lg:col-span-2 space-y-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-800 sm:text-base">
          <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-semibold text-ink-950">Hard wax vs soft wax</h2>
          <p>
            Soft wax is spread thin and removed with a strip, pulling from the skin. Hard wax is applied thick, then hardens
            as it cools, wrapping each hair so it can be pulled from the root <em>without</em> a strip — and without gripping
            the skin the same way. The result is less irritation, which is why
            <strong class="text-ink-950">hard wax Albuquerque</strong> is the go-to choice for sensitive areas.
          </p>
          <p>
            Hard wax is the professional standard for Brazilian and underarm work. It performs better on coarse, dense hair,
            and it can be reapplied to the same spot without the skin trauma of a strip. For large areas like legs, soft wax
            remains faster and is often the practical choice — so most strong menus carry both.
          </p>
          <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-semibold text-ink-950">Best practices and aftercare</h2>
          <p>
            Hair should be about a quarter inch so the wax can wrap it fully. After the service, keep the area clean and dry,
            skip heat and friction for a day, and exfoliate lightly after forty-eight hours to keep pores clear.
          </p>
          <p>
            Technique matters as much as product. A name that signals the method — like
            <strong class="text-ink-950">ABQWax.ing</strong> — helps a studio communicate expertise before a client ever walks in.
            See the <a href="/brazilian-wax-albuquerque/" class="font-medium text-gold-500 underline-offset-4 hover:underline">Brazilian wax guide</a>
            for how hard wax applies to that service.
          </p>
        </div>
        <aside class="rounded-3xl border border-ink-100 bg-ink-50 p-6 sm:p-8">
          <p class="text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-widestx text-gold-500">The domain</p>
          <p class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl font-semibold text-ink-950">ABQWax.ing</p>
          <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-700">City, category, and the .ing verb in one name. A domain that reads as the service itself.</p>
          <p class="mt-4 font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-gold-500">$250,000</p>
          <a href="#acquisition" class="btn-primary mt-4">Request terms</a>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-padding bg-ink-50">
      <div class="container-narrow">
        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl font-semibold text-ink-950 sm:text-4xl">Hard wax questions, answered</h2>
        <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <article class="card">
            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink-950">Is hard wax less painful?</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-700">Generally yes — it grips the hair rather than the skin, so it pulls less on the surface.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="card">
            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink-950">Where is hard wax used?</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-700">Brazilian, bikini, underarm, and facial areas — anywhere skin is thin or sensitive.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="card">
            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink-950">How long does it last?</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-700">Three to four weeks, since hair is removed from the root.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="card">
            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-semibold text-ink-950">Can it be reapplied?</h3>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-700">Yes — hard wax can be reapplied to the same area, which makes it ideal for coarse or stubborn hair.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
